              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 25,
                "start": 25
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Ms. Kruger, in civil contempt proceedings to enforce child\u2011support, due process requires a meaningful opportunity to be heard on whether the nonpaying parent has the ability to pay."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Bibas",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "ca2fa0b8bae823d3aeaf15c67d7d10d1b93024194055e8f5019654faea95b78a",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-ca2fa0b8bae8-0002-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 39,
                "start": 39
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Bibas, trial judges need to know ahead of time which set of procedures to apply, civil or criminal."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "MR. WAXMAN",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "ca2fa0b8bae823d3aeaf15c67d7d10d1b93024194055e8f5019654faea95b78a",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-ca2fa0b8bae8-0003-0007"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 61,
                "start": 61
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to MR. WAXMAN, the petitioner could be incarcerated and placed on work\u2011release in a county jail program to reduce his arrearage."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "MR. BIBAS",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "ca2fa0b8bae823d3aeaf15c67d7d10d1b93024194055e8f5019654faea95b78a",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-ca2fa0b8bae8-0003-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 57,
                "start": 57
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to MR. BIBAS, it is not necessary to have a lawyer because the issue is not that complex."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "MR. BIBAS",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "ca2fa0b8bae823d3aeaf15c67d7d10d1b93024194055e8f5019654faea95b78a",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-ca2fa0b8bae8-0003-0005"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 58,
                "start": 58
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to MR. BIBAS, the closest analogue is the inability to afford counsel under the Criminal Justice Act."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "MR. WAXMAN",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "ca2fa0b8bae823d3aeaf15c67d7d10d1b93024194055e8f5019654faea95b78a",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-ca2fa0b8bae8-0003-0009"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 62,
                "start": 62
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to MR. WAXMAN, the answer is yes, but a mere assertion is insufficient; the judge must see evidentiary support."
        }
      ],
